  "doc": {
    "description": "SR16 sequential building blocks (ISA.md §5).\n\nTwo-phase master-slave discipline: the master latch captures while Phi1 is\nhigh (gated by the load enable), the slave publishes while Phi2 is high.\nWith non-overlapping phases driven by the harness there is no race-through\nwindow: whatever the master holds when Phi1 falls is what the slave exposes\non the next Phi2 — edge-triggered behavior from level-sensitive latches.",
